The big local gain is more likely to come from reducing propagated sampling error. I’m testing moment matching next: normalize the Sobol normal probes to exact input mean/variance, and optionally force the first hidden layer’s sample marginals to their exact ReLU Gaussian mean/variance before forwarding deeper layers.
